(async () => {
  try {
    // Register the commands in the guild (local testing) or globally (production)
    // Replace 'yourGuildId' with the actual server ID if testing locally
    const registerResult = await rest.put(
      Routes.applicationGuildCommands(clientId, guildId || 'yourGuildId'),
      { body: commands },
    );

    console.log(`Successfully registered ${commands.length} command(s)`);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(error);
  }
})();
```

5. Launch the bot:
a. Add the following code at the bottom of `index.js` to launch the bot:

```javascript
DiscordClient.on('ready', () => {
  console.log(`Logged in as ${DiscordClient.user.tag}!`);
});

DiscordClient.on('interactionCreate', async interaction => {
  if (!interaction.isCommand()) return;

  if (interaction.commandName === 'ban') {
    await banInteraction(interaction);
  }
});

DiscordClient.login(token).catch(console.error);
```

7. Run the bot: In the project directory, run `node index.js` to start the bot. It will connect to Discord using the specified token and register the ban command.

